1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:01,420
I remember I felt so insecure.
我记得当时非常不自在，也没什么自信。

2
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:04,360
I literally went back to my mom. I was like, Mom, don't pack me those dumplings.
我回去就对妈妈说，别再给我带那些饺子了。

3
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:06,579
And I feel so bad. She must have been so confused.
现在想起来很难过，她当时一定很困惑。

4
00:00:06,579 --> 00:00:09,519
But me as a middle school kid, I just wanted to fit in.
但那时还是中学生的我，只想融入大家。

5
00:00:09,519 --> 00:00:14,500
And having like those kids say that, it just made me feel really awful because I felt like I don't belong.
同学那样说，让我很难受，觉得自己不属于那里。

6
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,380
I feel like I shouldn't stand out because I already don't belong.
我觉得自己本来就不合群，更不该太显眼。

7
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:20,620
And so if I even stand out, it just emphasizes the fact that I don't belong.
如果再显得不同，好像就更加突出我不合群这件事。

8
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:24,400
So I would lower myself, fit into that image that was already presented for me.
所以我会压低自己的存在感，去迎合别人已经给我的那种形象。

9
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:27,750
I was very focused on my academics. I wouldn't wear makeup. I wouldn't wear certain clothes.
我把注意力放在学习上，不化妆，也不穿某些衣服。

10
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:34,610
Because I didn't have a good support group. I didn't have like a supportive friend group or a certain community that would be like.
因为当时没有能支持我的朋友圈，也没有那样的群体。

11
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:39,160
But when I got to college, I changed my personality. I, I made a friend group.
到了大学，我开始改变自己的表现，也有了一个朋友圈。

12
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:42,940
I was more like embracing myself because I wanted to fit into a group so bad.
我开始更多展现自己，但也很想融入一个群体。

13
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:45,820
Those friends that I had were not that compatible to begin with.
可那些朋友和我，一开始就未必那么合拍。

14
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,680
We didn't share a lot of the same values.
我们有不少价值观并不一致。

15
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:51,940
Towards like, you know, like sophomore, junior year, I realized that maybe I just don't need to fit in.
大二、大三左右，我开始意识到，或许不必非得融入。

16
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,720
I, I really wish that I could sit here and be like, it's okay to not belong anywhere.
我很希望能坐在这里坦然地说，不属于任何群体也没关系。

17
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,060
Even now I'm still trying to deal with it because it gets lonely.
即使现在，我也还在慢慢面对，因为确实会感到孤单。

18
00:00:58,060 --> 00:01:00,400
And this year I really tried to meet more people.
今年我也在认真尝试认识更多人。

19
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,820
I'm also more introverted in this sense, so it's also kind of hard for me.
这方面我又比较内向，所以对我来说并不容易。

20
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:07,780
I am trying, and I feel this, it also goes to the fact that I'm a pretty awkward person too.
我在尝试，而且我也觉得，自己有时确实有点不自在。

21
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:12,870
I do find in certain social settings, but sometimes it's just, I also get pretty anxious for social settings.
有些社交场合我能应对，但有时也会很紧张。

22
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:17,799
Even when you do belong into like a certain group, you feel like an imposter. You feel like a fraud.
即使加入了某个群体，也可能觉得自己像是在装，像个冒名者。

23
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:23,079
It's almost like you feel like you need to create the sense of person in order to fit in with other people.
好像必须塑造某种样子，才能和别人合得来。

24
00:01:23,079 --> 00:01:27,459
When you grow up as a kid not fitting with your peers, it gets harder when you become an adult.
如果小时候就很难融入同龄人，成年后这件事也可能更难。

25
00:01:27,459 --> 00:01:30,700
And then you, you try to fit in and then you find that to be exhausting.
后来继续努力融入，却又觉得很累。

26
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,280
And then you came to the conclusion that maybe you just don't need to fit in.
再后来，你可能得出结论：也许不必非得融入。

27
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:35,440
But then when you don't need to fit it, it makes you feel free alone.
可当不再急着融入时，又可能同时感到自由和孤单。

28
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:41,739
Before I was always like, I don't need to fit in. Who needs to fit in? Like, I want to do my own thing.
以前我总说，不合群又怎样，我想做自己的事。

29
00:01:41,739 --> 00:01:44,859
But at the same time, I really want to be open to other people, or even like a place.
但同时，我也想对其他人、对某个地方保持开放。

30
00:01:44,859 --> 00:01:46,359
I don't know where exactly I belong to.
我还不知道自己的位置究竟在哪里。

31
00:01:46,359 --> 00:01:51,509
The lesson here that I've learned is the fact that if I did belong I don't think I would have done social media.
这段经历让我明白，如果当时有归属感，我也许就不会开始做社交媒体。

32
00:01:51,519 --> 00:01:54,639
Basically back then I used to expand on my private Snapchat story.
当时，我经常在自己的私密 Snapchat 动态里分享。

33
00:01:54,639 --> 00:01:58,959
And then I felt like annoying, even though I didn't force anyone to click on it. People just click on it, but I still feel bad.
虽然没人被强迫去看，我还是担心那些动态会打扰别人。

34
00:01:58,959 --> 00:02:04,359
So I just started spamming on my Tick Tock. So here I am making YouTube now, and I post on Instagram too.
后来我开始在 TikTok 频繁发内容，现在也做 YouTube、发 Instagram。

35
00:02:04,359 --> 00:02:08,500
So generally if I fit in, I don't think I would have posted on social media.
所以，如果那时更合群，我可能就不会在网上发内容了。

36
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,780
I wasn't in a friend group. Like nobody was gonna make fun of me.
当时没有固定朋友圈，也就少了害怕被熟人取笑的顾虑。

37
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:12,760
I was like, there's nothing to lose. I'll just post whatever.
我就想，也没什么可失去的，那就先发吧。

38
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:17,859
I think that was kind of like a bit of the start where I kind of realized the fact that I don't need to belong.
那大概是我开始意识到，不必强求归属感的起点。

39
00:02:17,859 --> 00:02:20,440
I'm just gonna do whatever. I'm not losing anything anyway. Like who cares?
我就先做自己想做的，反正也没损失，何必那么在意呢？

40
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:23,260
I do want to meet people that I share a genuine connection with.
我确实想认识那些能真诚相处的人。

41
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:26,079
I want to keep building my own little community of people.
我想继续慢慢建立属于自己的小小社群。

42
00:02:26,079 --> 00:02:31,949
This is something I struggled with my entire life. Um, I feel like I've never belonged anymore, and it's scary.
归属感是我一直在面对的问题。总觉得找不到位置，有时也会害怕。

43
00:02:31,959 --> 00:02:37,359
But, um, the thing that I can tell you is that stop trying, stop trying to belong, because it gets exhausting.
作者想说的是，不必一直用力追求融入，那样会很累。

44
00:02:37,359 --> 00:02:44,009
When you don't belong, you can't get yourself to belong somewhere.
如果感觉不属于那里，也很难勉强自己产生归属感。

45
00:02:44,019 --> 00:02:48,160
So when you stop trying to belong, you'll eventually find the place of where you belong.
她希望，当不再勉强自己时，能慢慢找到合适的位置。

46
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:50,320
Just be yourself. Be yourself, do your thing.
做自己，去做自己喜欢的事。

47
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:54,519
Because it's so easy to just fake away into being with people that you don't actually want to be with.
因为有时很容易迎合一个自己并不真正喜欢的群体。

48
00:02:54,519 --> 00:03:01,720
When you address yourself, you're gonna attract people who you feel like, oh my God, like I actually genuinely like hang out with this person. It makes me feel really great about myself.
她觉得，自然展现自己，更可能遇到相处舒服、让自己感觉良好的人。

49
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:06,160
That's my note to you guys. So yeah, I hope this video spoke to some of you guys and also helped some of you guys.
这些就是我想分享的话，希望这段视频让你有所共鸣，也能帮到一些人。

50
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:10,000
This is my journal entry number four to anyone who feel like they don't belong.
这是我的第四篇随笔，写给那些觉得自己不合群的人。

51
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:18,740
I will see you guys all next week. Yeah, bye.
下周再见，拜拜。
